# UI-106 review: fix flaky client-feature-routes-browser test

## Defect

`tests/client-feature-routes-browser.test.mjs` fails intermittently
(~3/55 runs, ~5%) at line 94:

    AssertionError: actual null, expected 'management'

The `open()` helper only waits for the fixture global function to exist
(`waitForGlobal` checks `typeof globalThis.inspectFeatureRoute === "function"`).
After `runFeatureNavigationScenario()` the browser sits on
`#/settings/runtime` with Local Operations mounted. `open('#/settings')`
navigates, and the very next statement calls
`inspectManagementPresentation('settings')`, which synchronously queries
`.wwc-settings`. Meanwhile `renderSettings()` is still awaiting the auth
restore + dynamic module import before it mounts the Settings page, so the
query returns `null`.

Every later step in the same test that goes through `settled()`/`waitFor`
on the selector never flakes — only the two synchronous
`inspectManagementPresentation` calls after `open()` are exposed.

Isolated repro: `review/ui106/verify-feature-routes-race.mjs` reproduces the
ordering gap (7/120 iterations observed `page=null`) using the same fixture
and the exact operations→settings navigation sequence.

## Minimal fix

Make `open()` also wait for the surface slot to settle before returning, by
reusing the in-page `waitFor` already exported by the fixture. One-line
change to the `open` helper; no assertions change.

```diff
--- a/tests/client-feature-routes-browser.test.mjs
+++ b/tests/client-feature-routes-browser.test.mjs
@@ -64,7 +64,9 @@
   async function open(path) {
     await devtools.send('Page.navigate', { url: `${clientOrigin}/${path}` }, sessionId)
     await waitForGlobal(devtools, sessionId, 'inspectFeatureRoute')
+    await evaluate(devtools, sessionId,
+      `globalThis.waitFor ? globalThis.waitFor(() => document.querySelector('.wwc-surface-slot section:not([hidden])') !== null, 'route slot') : true`)
   }
```

Note: the fixture currently keeps `waitFor` module-private. Equivalent
one-line alternative that needs no fixture change — poll through the already
global `inspectFeatureRoute`-family helpers is not possible for the
management pages, so export `waitFor` from
`tests/fixtures/browser-client-feature-routes.mjs`:

```diff
--- a/tests/fixtures/browser-client-feature-routes.mjs
+++ b/tests/fixtures/browser-client-feature-routes.mjs
@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@
-async function waitFor(predicate, label) {
+globalThis.waitFor = async function waitFor(predicate, label) {
```

Both diffs are against the candidate worktree files (untracked in this
branch). Apply there if the team prefers fixing the test alongside the
feature; the review worktree keeps only this record.
